{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 4, "model_name": "google/gemma-3n-e4b-it", "content": "## Lost (and Found) in Japan\n\nJapan. The word itself conjures images of ancient temples, bustling cityscapes, and serene gardens. My recent trip delivered on all fronts and then some!\n\nI started in Tokyo, a sensory overload in the best way. Shibuya Crossing was a must-see – a chaotic ballet of pedestrians. I explored quirky Harajuku, indulging in colorful street food, and found moments of peace in the Meiji Jingu Shrine. The food scene was incredible, from Michelin-starred restaurants to tiny ramen shops tucked away in alleyways.\n\nNext, I took the Shinkansen (bullet train!) to Kyoto. The contrast was striking. Kyoto felt steeped in history, with geishas gracefully gliding through Gion and stunning temples like Kinkaku-ji (the Golden Pavilion). I wandered through bamboo forests in Arashiyama, feeling utterly transported.\n\nBeyond the major cities, I loved the small details: the impeccable politeness of everyone I met, the artistry of the packaging, and the quiet beauty of the meticulously maintained gardens. \n\nIt wasn't always easy navigating the language barrier, but smiles and gestures went a long way. I got wonderfully lost (and happily found) in the vibrant culture. Japan is a country that truly captivates the soul.  I'm already dreaming of my return!\n\n\n\n", "logprobs": [{"token": "##", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": "▁Lost", "logprob": -0.0011843579122796655}, {"token": "▁(", "logprob": -0.16028544306755066}, {"token": "and", "logprob": -1.0728830375228426e-06}, {"token": "▁Found", "logprob": -0.0018123644404113293}, {"token": ")", "logprob": -0.14268149435520172}, {"token": "▁in", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": "▁Japan", "logprob": -0.07544055581092834}, {"token": "\n\n", "logprob": -0.21004177629947662}, {"token": "Japan", "logprob": -0.5764119029045105}, {"token": ".", "logprob": -0.011837475933134556}, {"token": "▁The", "log